  "notes": "The best kind of door step in the corpus: 'Door: Prince Royal's Rm' is a real, targetable entity and the normaliser already folds it to the client's 'Door:Name' form, so step 1 carries a marker where v1 could only point at Prince Trion. The header puts him at (H-8) and the walkthrough puts the door at (H-7); both are kept where each was written rather than reconciled. 'Quest Reqs: San d'Oria Rank 2 -or- Bastok/Windurst Rank 3' has no slot in the schema and no observable predicate, so it is flagged and gates nothing. Bullet 2 ('the rest can be done as any job') is a note on the job gate, not a step; the runtime already gets that right for free, since prereq.evaluate only runs for quests you have not started. Note this Exoroche is the San d'Oria one -- the same name is an Abyssea - La Theine NPC in 'The Angling Armorer', and only the zone separates them.\n\nMoved out of the player-facing step notes (build vocabulary; see AUTHORING.md, 'Two notes, two audiences'):\n  step 5: the key is 5,000 gil from the Curio Vendor Moogle with Rhapsody in Umber, or drops from the demons; a Thief can pick the lock instead, which is why items_partial is set",
