  "notes": "Eighteen bullets, of which about half are routing advice through Arrapago Reef rather than steps. The page contradicts itself about the final ???: bullet 11 says Caedarva Mire (K-5) and bullet 17 says (K-6). Both are recorded in the note and (K-6) is used, because bullet 17 is the one giving the instruction; the quest is demoted to medium for it. There is no hand-in NPC at all -- the quest ends on a cutscene at the ??? -- so the last step is deliberately unmarkable and no turn-in can ever be claimed, which is the honest answer rather than pointing at Iruki-Waraki again. Step 2 is the one genuine AND-list here: Sleeping Potion and Chai together.\n\nMoved out of the player-facing step notes (build vocabulary; see AUTHORING.md, 'Two notes, two audiences'):\n  step 6: A Thief can lockpick the gate instead, or farm the key from lamia and draugar inside the reef, which is why items_partial is set.",
